VERDICT
==============================================================================================================
  With no free parameter, the framework puts RC100's median dark fraction within 0.07 on its worst systematic cell.
  LCDM's best cell per variant misses by: NFW 0.02, H 0.00, C 0.00, K 0.03, A 0.17, ALL 0.10 (ALL = halo mass -0.2 dex,
  concentration -0.1 dex, and a maximal feedback core together).  THE LEVEL IS A TIE (yes): L320's "framework
  beats LCDM on the dark fractions" is WITHDRAWN.  THE TREND: LCDM's least-rising cell sits 3.7 sigma above RC100's
  d log a0/dz; the framework is flat, 1.6 sigma from it.
  Caveats that no model choice here removes: RC100's f_DM comes from its own mass models (stellar M/L, gas from scaling
  relations, pressure support), and its selection across redshift is not controlled.  This is a relative statement --
  same baryons, same radii, two gravity models -- and it is quoted as such.

  6/6 checks pass; load-bearing failures: 0; wrote L323_rc100_framework_vs_lcdm_stress_results.json
